---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Focus Pet"
  description="How Focus Pet handles your data."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-16">
      <a href="/" class="font-heading font-semibold text-text-secondary no-underline hover:text-accent-blue">
        &larr; Back to Home
      </a>

      <div class="mt-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold md:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-text-secondary">Last updated August 20, 2026.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8 text-text-secondary">
        <p>
          Focus Pet is designed to be a local-first focus and productivity application. This Privacy Policy
          explains what information Focus Pet processes, what information may be stored or synchronized, and
          how third-party services are used.
        </p>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Information We Collect and Process</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            The information Focus Pet processes depends on the features you choose to use.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 font-heading text-base font-bold text-text-primary">Account Information</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Creating an account is optional. If you create a Focus Pet account, we may process information such
            as:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>your email address;</li>
            <li>authentication information necessary to sign you in and maintain your account;</li>
            <li>account and session information necessary to keep your account signed in securely;</li>
            <li>a device identifier used to manage Focus Pet's single-active-device account system.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You can use Focus Pet in guest mode without creating an account. Guest mode does not use cloud
            backup.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 font-heading text-base font-bold text-text-primary">
            Focus and Productivity Information
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-2">During a focus session, Focus Pet may process information such as:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>the active application and its application identifier;</li>
            <li>the active website domain when using a supported browser;</li>
            <li>your allowed and blocked applications;</li>
            <li>your allowed and blocked website domains;</li>
            <li>focus-session duration and completion status;</li>
            <li>distraction and restricted-event counts;</li>
            <li>focus mode and related session settings;</li>
            <li>rewards, streaks, and focus statistics derived from your sessions.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            This information is used to determine whether your current activity matches the focus rules you
            selected and to provide Focus Pet's focus-session, reward, statistics, and Deep Focus features.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">
            How Application and Website Detection Works
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pet needs to determine which application is currently active while a focus session is
            running.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            On supported browsers, Focus Pet may also determine the domain of the website currently active in
            the browser so that website Allow Lists and Block Lists can work.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Depending on your operating system, Focus Pet uses operating-system functionality such as Windows
            application APIs or macOS Accessibility APIs to perform this detection.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">Focus Pet does <strong class="text-text-primary">not</strong> use this functionality to read or collect:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>the contents of your files or documents;</li>
            <li>the contents of webpages;</li>
            <li>text you enter into applications or websites;</li>
            <li>passwords or other personal credentials;</li>
            <li>private messages;</li>
            <li>keystrokes;</li>
            <li>screenshots;</li>
            <li>screen recordings.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet's website rules operate on domains rather than storing full browsing URLs. For example,
            Focus Pet may use <code class="rounded bg-surface px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm">youtube.com</code>
            to evaluate a website rule rather than storing the full page URL you visited.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Application and website detection is used for Focus Pet's focus features and is not intended to
            create a general browsing or computer-activity history.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Local Storage</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pet is designed to work locally on your computer, including in guest mode.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Application data may be stored locally using Focus Pet's local database and other local application
            storage. Depending on the features you use, locally stored information may include:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>game progress and currencies;</li>
            <li>streaks and focus statistics;</li>
            <li>completed focus-session information;</li>
            <li>pets and selected skins;</li>
            <li>inventory and decorations;</li>
            <li>backyard configuration;</li>
            <li>focus settings;</li>
            <li>allowed and blocked applications;</li>
            <li>allowed and blocked website domains;</li>
            <li>Focus Pro entitlement information cached for offline use;</li>
            <li>other settings required for application functionality.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Cloud Backup and Accounts</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If you choose to create and use a Focus Pet account, Focus Pet can back up supported game and
            settings data to the cloud so that your progress can be restored when you sign in on a supported
            device.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">Cloud backup may include information such as:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>game progress and currencies;</li>
            <li>streak and focus totals;</li>
            <li>pet information and selected skin;</li>
            <li>owned skins;</li>
            <li>inventory;</li>
            <li>backyard/decorations;</li>
            <li>focus settings;</li>
            <li>allowed and blocked application identifiers;</li>
            <li>allowed and blocked website domains.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet accounts currently use a single-active-device model. You may use your account on different
            devices over time, but only one device may hold the active authenticated Focus Pet session at a
            time.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            A persistent installation identifier may be used to identify the Focus Pet installation
            participating in this account-session system.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Cloud backup is optional. If you do not create an account, you can continue using Focus Pet in guest
            mode without cloud backup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Focus Pro and Payments</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Focus Pet offers optional paid Focus Pro plans.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Payments and subscription billing are handled through
            <strong class="text-text-primary">Stripe</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When you choose to purchase Focus Pro, Focus Pet may open Stripe Checkout in your web browser.
            Subscription management, payment-method management, and billing information may also be handled
            through Stripe's Customer Portal.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Stripe is responsible for processing payment information and managing billing events such as
            purchases, subscriptions, renewals, cancellations, and payment failures.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet uses verified billing information from Stripe to determine whether an account has Focus
            Pro access. Focus Pet's cloud services store the resulting entitlement and subscription status
            needed to provide Focus Pro features, and the desktop application may keep a local cached copy so
            entitlement information can remain available offline.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet does not need to directly store your full payment-card details in its own application
            database.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pet currently uses third-party service providers including:
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-6 font-heading text-base font-bold text-text-primary">Supabase</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">Supabase is used for features including:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>account authentication;</li>
            <li>cloud backup and restore;</li>
            <li>account/session coordination;</li>
            <li>Focus Pro entitlement information;</li>
            <li>server-side functions that support Focus Pro billing workflows.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="mt-6 font-heading text-base font-bold text-text-primary">Stripe</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">Stripe is used for:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>Focus Pro Checkout;</li>
            <li>recurring subscription billing;</li>
            <li>one-time Focus Pro purchases where offered;</li>
            <li>payment processing;</li>
            <li>subscription status;</li>
            <li>payment-method management;</li>
            <li>billing and subscription management through Stripe's Customer Portal.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3">
            These providers may process information according to their own privacy policies and terms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">How We Use Information</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">We use information processed by Focus Pet to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>provide focus-session functionality;</li>
            <li>evaluate the Allow Lists and Block Lists you configure;</li>
            <li>provide Normal Focus and Deep Focus behavior;</li>
            <li>calculate rewards, streaks, and focus statistics;</li>
            <li>save your game progress and settings;</li>
            <li>synchronize supported data when you choose to use a Focus Pet account;</li>
            <li>authenticate and maintain your account;</li>
            <li>manage Focus Pro access;</li>
            <li>provide and maintain application functionality;</li>
            <li>provide customer support;</li>
            <li>diagnose bugs and improve reliability and stability;</li>
            <li>protect account and service security.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">We do not sell your personal information.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">
            Information We Do Not Intend to Collect
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2">Focus Pet is not designed to collect or store:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>the contents of your documents or files;</li>
            <li>webpage contents;</li>
            <li>full browsing history;</li>
            <li>full browsing URLs as focus-rule history;</li>
            <li>passwords entered into other applications or websites;</li>
            <li>private messages;</li>
            <li>keystrokes;</li>
            <li>screenshots;</li>
            <li>screen recordings.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Operating-system permissions used for focus detection are used to provide Focus Pet's focus
            functionality and are not intended for general surveillance of your computer activity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Data Retention</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We retain account and cloud data for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the Focus Pet
            services you use, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, enforce agreements, and maintain
            service security.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Local data may remain on a device until it is removed through Focus Pet, the application's available
            account/data controls, or removal of the application's local data.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Some information processed by third-party providers such as Stripe or Supabase may also be retained
            according to their applicable legal obligations, retention practices, and privacy policies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Your Choices and Rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding your personal information, including the
            right to:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
            <li>request access to personal information associated with your account;</li>
            <li>request correction of inaccurate personal information;</li>
            <li>request deletion of eligible account information;</li>
            <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent;</li>
            <li>exercise other privacy rights available under applicable law.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">
            You may also choose to use Focus Pet without creating an account, in which case cloud backup and
            account-based features are not used.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To make a privacy request, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:help@tryfocuspet.com">help@tryfocuspet.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Security</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We use reasonable technical and organizational measures intended to protect information from
            unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Focus Pet's architecture is designed to keep sensitive desktop activity processing limited to what
            is necessary for focus functionality, and cloud account access is subject to authentication and
            access controls.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            However, no method of electronic storage or transmission over the internet can be guaranteed to be
            completely secure.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Focus Pet is not intended to knowingly collect personal information from children in violation of
            applicable law.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you believe a child has provided personal information to Focus Pet in circumstances where it
            should not have been collected, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:help@tryfocuspet.com">help@tryfocuspet.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">We may update this Privacy Policy as Focus Pet changes.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            When we make changes, we will update the <strong class="text-text-primary">Last updated</strong>
            date at the top of this page. If a change materially affects how personal information is handled,
            we may provide additional notice where appropriate.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-heading text-lg font-bold text-text-primary">Contact Us</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, how Focus Pet handles information, or a privacy
            request, contact:
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a href="mailto:help@tryfocuspet.com">help@tryfocuspet.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
